# HOST ROLES -- THE AUTHORITATIVE HOST POPULATION (operator ruling 2026-08-29).
# ~/.config/bd/hosts is DERIVED from this file. Until 2026-08-29 hosts listed 7
# of the 12 real machines, so every fleet claim made that day was against a
# wrong denominator and five machines were invisible. Roles carries the role,
# so roles is the source; hosts carries only name and ip for tools that read it.
#
# roles:
#   integrator  sole writer. worktrees, cuts, merges. NEVER a deploy target.
#   runner      runs BD and carries scheduled load
#   deploy      receives scripts/deploy.sh from bd-fleet-deploy.sh
#   capacity    NO BD. bands, captures and agent work only. Never deployed to.
#
# BANDS RUN ON `capacity` AND `runner`, NEVER ON `deploy` OR THE INTEGRATOR.
# Added 2026-08-31. bd-band-remote.sh used to `git checkout --detach` in the
# host's own BulkDownloader, which would move a serving host off main and
# destroy its deploy provenance -- so only non-serving boxes could be listed.
# Each band now runs in its own per-SHA worktree and never touches the host
# checkout, so a runner can lend cores while it serves. DO NOT RENAME `runner`
# TO ADD BAND CAPACITY: bd-fleet-deploy.sh holds back hosts whose role is
# exactly `runner`, so renaming one silently turns it into a deploy target.
#
# bd-fleet-deploy.sh targets `deploy` and `runner`. A MISSING OR UNREADABLE
# ROLES FILE DEPLOYS EVERYWHERE, deliberately -- so keep this file readable.
integrator test5 10.0.70.164
runner   test2 10.0.70.95
runner   test3 10.0.70.80
runner   test6 10.0.70.249
deploy   test  10.0.70.83
deploy   test4 10.0.70.85
deploy   test7 10.0.70.84
# 2026-08-29: bd and bd1 PROMOTED to deploy targets by operator ruling, which
# SUPERSEDES the 2026-08-28 comment that said bd-fleet-deploy must never touch
# these five. They were found running v3.66.1326 and v3.66.1327 -- about twenty
# versions behind main and predating every download fix of 2026-08-29. Their
# downloads stay STOPPED until row 388 lands, same hold as test6.
deploy   bd    10.0.70.50
deploy   bd1   10.0.70.51
# CAPACITY, NOT DEPLOY. 48cpu/344GB each, no BD on 5555. Operator 2026-08-29:
# may be wiped and rebuilt freely. Used for bands, captures and agent work so
# that measurement is not run on the tree the integrator is editing (A6).
capacity bd2   10.0.70.52
# RESERVED 2026-08-31 for an operator ultrareview session. bd-band-remote
# selects `capacity` and `runner`, so this word takes bd3 OUT of the band
# population entirely. Belt and braces: the lane ALSO refuses any host running
# a claude/codex process (bd-band-remote.sh:128-130), so a live session already
# makes bd3 unavailable -- but that guard fires at dispatch time, and a band
# already in flight would contend. This word means no band can ever start.
# RESTORE TO `capacity` WHEN THE REVIEW IS DONE.
reserved bd3   10.0.70.53
capacity bd4   10.0.70.54
